WEBVTT

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:03.348
Second Grain begins with a simple question.

00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:06.771
How can reclaimed timber shape a new design?

00:00:07.216 --> 00:00:10.155
We start with real Earthwise listings.

00:00:10.371 --> 00:00:15.534
Seller photographs, dimensions, and quantities remain linked to their source.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.784
You set the brief. The agent proposes changes for your review.

00:00:21.245 --> 00:00:24.549
The allocation retains each bar's identity.

00:00:24.793 --> 00:00:30.562
This example shows two installed parts, the saw cuts, and the remaining length.

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:34.755
Each piece keeps its original position along the source bar.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.543
The original mixed integer solver matches the confirmed design to the available stock.

00:00:41.175 --> 00:00:45.389
Watch the recorded pieces move from their source bars into the model.

00:00:46.021 --> 00:00:50.720
This is a replay of a saved allocation, not a new calculation.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.189
Eighty-seven source bars supply one hundred and fifty-five installed parts.

00:00:56.606 --> 00:01:01.220
The model retains every source link, cut, and remainder.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:09.978
Finally, inspect the saved Karamba analysis: fifteen load cases, support reactions, and member forces.

00:01:10.265 --> 00:01:13.534
Red lines show exaggerated deformation.

00:01:13.821 --> 00:01:18.889
The maximum recorded translation is eighteen point zero five millimetres.

00:01:19.176 --> 00:01:23.220
This remains preliminary, not structural approval.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.974
From recovered stock to a traceable assembly.

00:01:27.331 --> 00:01:29.720
Every piece keeps its story.
